                             Power:** `TSREF` (Thermistor Reference) connects to the `PULLUP` rail via jumper **J5**.\n   151\t*   **Divider Network:** The `PULLUP`             
                             rail feeds 8 parallel voltage dividers. Each divider consists of a 10.0k top resistor (e.g., R7) and a bottom NTC thermistor (e.g.,                 
                             RT1) to GND.\n   152\t*   **Measurement Points:** The midpoint of each divider is labeled `GPIOx_R` (e.g., `GPIO8_R`, `GPIO7_R`...                  
                             `GPIO1_R`).\n   153\t*   **GPIO Interface (J4):**\n   154\t    *   **J4** allows connecting the BMS IC's `GPIOx` pins (odd pins 1-15)               
                             to the measurement points.\n   155\t    *   **Channels 2-8:** `GPIOx` connects directly to `GPIOx_R` when the jumper is placed.\n                   
                             156\t    *   **Channel 1:** Unlike channels 2-8, Channel 1 includes an intermediate filter stage. The divider node `GPIO1_R` (with C60              
                             and D3) connects via R128 (1k) to `GPIO1_C`. `GPIO1_C` then connects to J4 Pin 2. Thus, the BMS pin `GPIO1` measures the filtered                   
                             divider voltage through a 1k series resistor.\n   157\t    *   **TP44** provides a test point on the `GPIO1_R` net (the divider                     
                             node).\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t# Uncertainties, Assumptions & Confidence\n   161\t\n   162\t*   **Assumption:** The numbers 12                 
                             through 16 in the configuration block represent the cell index in the stack.\n   163\t*   **Uncertainty:** The destination of the                   
