t by creating the basic structure of the `tscircuit` file. I'll define the `board` and the main IC `U1` (BQ79616PAPR). I'll also define the main nets like `GND`, `PWR`, `AVDD`, `CVDD`, `DVDD`, `TSREF`, `LDOIN`, `NEG5V`.\n\nAccording to BFS-DC, I should start with the structural anchors. U1 is the most central component.\n\nI'll create the file `/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/output/bq79616_eval_board.tsx`.\n"}}, 'thoughtSignature': 'c2tpcF90aG91Z2h0X3NpZ25hdHVyZV92YWxpZGF0b3I='}, {'function_call': {'name': 'file_editor', 'args': {'file_text': 'import { BQ79616PAPR } from "./lib/BQ79616PAPR"\n\nexport default () => {\n  return (\n    <board width="200mm" height="150mm">\n      <net name="GND" />\n      <net name="PWR" />\n      <net name="AVDD" />\n      <net name="CVDD" />\n      <net name="DVDD" />\n      <net name="TSREF" />\n      <net name="LDOIN" />\n      <net name="NEG5V" />\n      <net name="NPNB" />\n      <net name="REFHP" />\n\n      <BQ79616PAPR name="U1" />\n\n      {/* Ground connections for U1 */}\n      <trace from=".U1 > .AVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .CVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .DVSS" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .REFHM" to="net.GND" />\n      <trace from=".U1 > .EP" to="net.GND" />\n\n    </board>\n  )\n}\n', 'security_risk': 'LOW', 'path': '/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/output/bq79616_eval_board.tsx', 'command': 'create'}}, 'thoughtSignature': 'c2tpcF90aG91Z2h0X3NpZ25hdHVyZV92YWxpZGF0b3I='}]}, {'parts': [{'function_response': {'name': 'think', 'response': {'content': 'Your thought has been logged.'}}}, {'function_response': {'name': 'file_editor', 'response': {'content': 'File created successfully at: /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/output/bq79616_eval_board.tsx'}}}]}, {'role': 'model', 'parts': [{'function_call': {'name': 'file_editor', 'args': {'security_risk': 'LOW', 'command': 'view', 'path': '/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/schematic_images/subckt_pow_supply.png'}}, 'thoughtSignature': 'c2tpcF90aG91Z2h0X3NpZ25hdHVyZV92YWxpZGF0b3I='}]}, {'parts': [{'function_response': {'name': 'file_editor', 'response': {'content': 'Image file /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/schematic_images/subckt_pow_supply.png read successfully. Displaying image content.'}}}]}, {'role': 'model', 'parts': [{'function_call': {'name': 'think', 'args': {'thought': "I will now add the power supply components: Q1, R3, R4, R5, C1, C2, C3, C5, C6, C7, C8, C9, C59.\nI'll also add the LED D1 and its resistor R121.\n\nFrom SCUD:\n- R5 (30.0Ω), C5 (10nF) on `BAT` pin.\n- Q1 Collector via R4 (200Ω) and R3 (100Ω) from `PWR`.\n- C1 (0.22μF) on Q1 Collector.\n- Q1 Emitter to `LDOIN`.\n- Q1 Base to `NPNB`.\n- AVDD: C6 (1μF)\n- CVDD: C9 (1μF)\n- DVDD: C7 (4.7μF), C8 (1μF)\n- LDOIN: C59 (0.1μF)\n- NEG5V: C3 (0.1μF)\n- TSREF: C2 (1μF)\n- D1 (LED) with R121 (1.0k) and J6.\n\nI need to check the pinout for MMBT3904LT1G (Q1).\nFrom component_pin_mapping.md:\nMMBT3904LT1G: pin1: pin1, pin2: pin2, pin3: pin3.\nWait, usually for SOT-23 MMBT3904: 1=Base, 2=Emitter, 3=Collector.\nLet me check the schematic image `subckt_pow_supply.png` to be sure about Q1 pins if possible, or assume standard SOT-23 if not specified.\nActually, the mapping says pin1, pin2, pin3. I should check if there's more info or just use them.\nLooking at `subckt_pow_supply.png`...\nQ1 is MMBT3904.\nPin 1 is Base (connected to NPNB).\nPin 2 is Emitter (connected to LDOIN).\nPin 3 is Collector (connected to R3).\nThis matches standard SOT-23.\n\nWait, I should also check the LED D1 pins.\n150060GS75000: pin1: K, pin2: A.\n\nI'll add these components now.\n"}}, 'thoughtSignature': 'c2tpcF90aG91Z2h0X3NpZ25hdHVyZV92YWxpZGF0b3I='}, {'function_call': {'name': 'file_editor', 'args': {'command': 'insert', 'new_str': '      {/* Power Supply Components */}\n      <resi