                                     "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"I will now add the power supply components: Q1, R3, R4, R5, C1, C2, C3, C5, C6, C7, C8, C9,                   
                             C59.\\nI'll also add the LED D1 and its resistor R121.\\n\\nFrom SCUD:\\n- R5 (30.0\u03a9), C5 (10nF) on `BAT` pin.\\n- Q1 Collector                
                             via R4 (200\u03a9) and R3 (100\u03a9) from `PWR`.\\n- C1 (0.22\u03bcF) on Q1 Collector.\\n- Q1 Emitter to `LDOIN`.\\n- Q1 Base to                   
                             `NPNB`.\\n- AVDD: C6 (1\u03bcF)\\n- CVDD: C9 (1\u03bcF)\\n- DVDD: C7 (4.7\u03bcF), C8 (1\u03bcF)\\n- LDOIN: C59 (0.1\u03bcF)\\n- NEG5V:             
                             C3 (0.1\u03bcF)\\n- TSREF: C2 (1\u03bcF)\\n- D1 (LED) with R121 (1.0k) and J6.\\n\\nI need to check the pinout for MMBT3904LT1G                     
                             (Q1).\\nFrom component_pin_mapping.md:\\nMMBT3904LT1G: pin1: pin1, pin2: pin2, pin3: pin3.\\nWait, usually for SOT-23 MMBT3904: 1=Base,             
                             2=Emitter, 3=Collector.\\nLet me check the schematic image `subckt_pow_supply.png` to be sure about Q1 pins if possible, or assume                  
                             standard SOT-23 if not specified.\\nActually, the mapping says pin1, pin2, pin3. I should check if there's more info or just use                    
                             them.\\nLooking at `subckt_pow_supply.png`...\\nQ1 is MMBT3904.\\nPin 1 is Base (connected to NPNB).\\nPin 2 is Emitter (connected to               
                             LDOIN).\\nPin 3 is Collector (connected to R3).\\nThis matches standard SOT-23.\\n\\nWait, I should also check the LED D1                           
                             pins.\\n150060GS75000: pin1: K, pin2: A.\\n\\nI'll add these components now.\\n\"}",                                                                
