\n- RT1-RT8: NCP18XH103F03RB.\\n- R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19: 10.0k.\\n\\nPin mapping for NCP18XH103F03RB: pin1, pin2.\\nPin mapping for BZX84C24: pin1: Anode, pin2: pin2, pin3: Cathode.\\nWait, BZX84C24 is a Zener. Usually pin 3 is Cathode, pin 1 is Anode.\\nThe mapping says pin1: Anode, pin2: pin2, pin3: Cathode.\\nSCUD says D3 is a \\"24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode\\".\\nLet\'s check `subckt_gpios.png` for D3.\\nD3 in `subckt_gpios.png` shows two Zeners common anode? Or common cathode?\\nActually, BZX84C24 is a single Zener. But SCUD says \\"Dual Zener/TVS\\".\\nWait, BZX84C24 is a single Zener in SOT-23 where pin 3 is Cathode and pin 1 is Anode (pin 2 is NC).\\nLet me check the image.\\nIn `subckt_gpios.png`, D3 is shown as a 3-pin device.\\nIt looks like a bidirectional TVS or two Zeners.\\nIf it\'s BZX84C24, it\'s a single Zener.\\nI\'ll follow the pin mapping: pin1: Anode, pin3: Cathode.\\n\\nI\'ll add these now.\\n"}'}}, {'id': 'call_362826f655cf45b1b2269cb7ae10', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'file_editor', 'arguments': '{"security_risk": "LOW", "new_str": "\\n      {/* Temperature Sensing Subsystem */}\\n      <net name=\\"PULLUP\\" />\\n      <jumper name=\\"J5\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\"net.TSREF\\" to=\\".J5 > .pin1\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".J5 > .pin2\\" to=\\"net.PULLUP\\" />\\n\\n      <import { NCP18XH103F03RB } from \\"./lib/NCP18XH103F03RB\\" />\\n      <import { BZX84C24 } from \\"./lib/BZX84C24\\" />\\n      <jumper name=\\"J4\\" /> {/* 2x8 Header */}\\n\\n      {/* Channel 1 with Filter */}\\n      <resistor name=\\"R7\\" resistance=\\"10k\\" footprint=\\"0603\\" />\\n      <NCP18XH103F03RB name=\\"RT1\\" />\\n      <resistor name=\\"R128\\" resistance=\\"1k\\" footprint=\\"0603\\" />\\n      <capacitor name=\\"C60\\" capacitance=\\"1uF\\" footprint=\\"0603\\" />\\n      <BZX84C24 name=\\"D3\\" />\\n      <net name=\\"GPIO1_R\\" />\\n      <net name=\\"GPIO1_C\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\"net.PULLUP\\" to=\\".R7 > .pin1\\" 