                             Header (USB2ANY / MCU Interface)\\n- J18: Connects `CVDD` to `CVDD_CO`\\n- J21: Connects `RX_CO` to `RX`\\n- J2: Connects `NFAULT` to               
                             `NF_J`\\n\\nSignal Flow:\\n- `USB2ANY_TX_3.3` (J17-7) -> U2 (INB) -> U2 (OUTB) -> `RX_CO` -> J21 -> `RX` (U1-52)\\n- `TX` (U1-53) -> U2             
                             (INC) -> U2 (OUTC) -> `USB2ANY_RX_3.3` (J17-8)\\n- `NFAULT` (U1-62) -> J2 -> `NF_J` -> U2 (IND) -> U2 (OUTD) -> `NFAULT_C`                          
                             (J17-3)\\n\\nPin mapping for ISO7342FCQDWRQ1:\\n- pin1: VCC1\\n- pin2: GND11\\n- pin3: INA\\n- pin4: INB\\n- pin5: OUTC\\n- pin6:                   
                             OUTD\\n- pin7: EN1\\n- pin8: GND12\\n- pin9: GND22\\n- pin10: EN2\\n- pin11: IND\\n- pin12: INC\\n- pin13: OUTB\\n- pin14: OUTA\\n-                 
                             pin15: GND21\\n- pin16: VCC2\\n\\nI'll also add the direct UART header J3 and J1.\\n- J3-1: GND\\n- J3-2: NFAULT\\n- J3-3: RX_C\\n-                 
                             J3-4: TX\\n- J1: Connects `RX_C` to `RX` via R119 (100\u03a9).\\n\\nWait, SCUD says: `RX` (BMS) can be driven from `RX_C` (J3-3) via                
                             R119 (100\u03a9) and J1.\\nSo: J3-3 -> R119 -> J1 -> RX.\\n\\nI'll add these now.\\n\"}",                                                           
